==English==

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hoax]], [[prank]] or [[jest]]
# A [[fraud]] or [[sham]]
# A [[fraudster]] or [[cheat]]
#{{British}} A type of [[chewy]] [[sweet]] ([[candy]])

===Interjection===
{{en-intj}}

# [[nonsense]]!
#* '''1843''', [[w:Charles Dickens|Charles Dickens]], ''[[w:A Christmas Carol|A Christmas Carol in Prose, Being a Ghost Story of Christmas]]'', [[s:A Christmas Carol/Stave 1|stave 1]],
#*: ‘A Merry Christmas, uncle! God save you!’ cried a cheerful voice. It was the voice of Scrooge’s nephew, who came upon him so quickly that this was the first intimation he had of his approach.
#*: ‘Bah!’ said Scrooge, ‘'''Humbug'''!’

===Verb===
{{en-verb|humbugs|humbugging|humbugged}}

# To play a [[trick]] on.
# To [[cheat]], [[swindle]].

====Usage notes====
* The spellings {{term|humbuging}} and {{term|humbuged}} exist, but are not nearly so common as {{term|humbugging}} and {{term|humbugged}}.

